# Store credentials for local publishing. Copy to .env.store (git-ignored) in either:
#   - this toolkit's folder: shared by every extension you publish from here, or
#   - an extension repo's root: for that extension only; wins over the shared file.
# Real environment variables win over both. Pipelines set secret variables instead.
# Setup steps for each value: README.md, "One-time store setup".

# ── Chrome Web Store (API v2, service account) ──
# The service account's JSON key file - one of these three:
CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_FILE=
# CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account",...}
# CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_EMAIL=
# CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# A relative key file path is relative to the folder holding this .env.store.

# ── Microsoft Edge Add-ons (API v1.1) ──
# Partner Center → Microsoft Edge → Publish API. The API key expires - note the date.
EDGE_CLIENT_ID=
EDGE_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: override the IDs in store/store.json (not secret) ──
# Only useful in an extension's own .env.store, e.g. to publish to a test listing.
# CHROME_EXTENSION_ID=
# CHROME_PUBLISHER_ID=
# EDGE_PRODUCT_ID=
